desc:
Discussion of the development and strategy to create a new school of Public Health that, within a decade, is ranked in the top third of all schools and programs in the country and has broad success metrics;
Presentation of the health and social challenges facing northeast Tennessee and southwest Virginia;
Explore the inter-relationship of health, economic development and education and the importance of collaborative efforts to address all three parameters.
Explore how the Center for Rural Health research will work with regional partners and national experts to execute a performance excellence strategy to impact these health and social conditions by interrupting the inter-generational cycles of poor health, lack of education, and poverty.
